💀 Alright, Bryan—you just stepped into the **classic “stray characters after delete” trap.**

Let me break it down fast and clean:

---

### 🔥 What Happened

You deleted lines 24, 25, and 26 *by selecting just the line numbers and maybe not the whole JSX block*—and as a result, your code now looks something like this:

```tsx
&lt;TabsList className=&quot;mb-4&quot;&gt;
  &lt;TabsTrigger value=&quot;dashboard&quot;&gt;Strategic Dashboard&lt;/TabsTrigger&gt;
  ...
&lt;/TabsList&gt;

&lt;div className=&quot;min-h-screen bg-black text-white p-6&quot;&gt;
```

And that’s the **problem**—because now you&#x27;ve got a random `&lt;div&gt;` hanging out **without a parent return** context.

---

### ✅ Here&#x27;s How to Fix It in Two Steps

#### 🧼 Step 1: Restore Your JSX Block
Put this back **exactly** like this (minus the line numbers):

```tsx
&lt;TabsContent value=&quot;dashboard&quot;&gt;
  &lt;Card&gt;
    &lt;CardContent className=&quot;space-y-4&quot;&gt;
      &lt;h2 className=&quot;text-2xl font-semibold&quot;&gt;Life Goals &amp; Strategic Timeline&lt;/h2&gt;
      &lt;ul className=&quot;list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-lg&quot;&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;Build Prometheus Prime to MVP&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;Launch strategic blog series&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;Master financial systems for autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;
      &lt;Button className=&quot;mt-4&quot; onClick={() =&gt; alert(&#x27;Goal adding coming soon!&#x27;)}&gt;
        + Add New Goal
      &lt;/Button&gt;
    &lt;/CardContent&gt;
  &lt;/Card&gt;
&lt;/TabsContent&gt;
```

#### 🧨 Step 2: Make Sure Your `return()` Block is Properly Wrapped
Your entire JSX should start and end inside one wrapper—like this:

```tsx
return (
  &lt;div className=&quot;min-h-screen bg-black text-white p-6&quot;&gt;
    {/* Everything goes inside this div */}
    &lt;h1 className=&quot;text-4xl font-bold mb-8&quot;&gt;Prometheus Prime&lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;Tabs defaultValue=&quot;dashboard&quot;&gt;
      &lt;TabsList className=&quot;mb-4&quot;&gt;
        ...
      &lt;/TabsList&gt;

      {/* All your TabsContent components go here */}
    &lt;/Tabs&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
)
```

You **can’t just delete JSX lines** without making sure the opening/closing tags match and the tree stays valid.

---

### 🧠 Double Check:
- Every `&lt;TabsContent&gt;` has a matching `&lt;/TabsContent&gt;`
- Every `&lt;Card&gt;` has a matching `&lt;/Card&gt;`
- No JSX is sitting outside the main `return (&lt;div&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;)` block

